  "raw": {
    "https://portals.williamwoods.edu/employment/job_details.aspx?id=584": {
      "title": "Professor of Communications",
      "description": "Job Details | William Woods University Skip to content Admissions\n                    Menu Job Details Job Title: Professor of Communications Department: School of Art, Design and Media Reports To: Dean of the School of Art, Design and Media Job Type: This is a full time, exempt position. General Description: William Woods University is accepting applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position to teach communication to undergraduate students. The contracted teaching load is 12 hours per semester, with the opportunity to teach additional courses as overload. Full-time faculty are expected to participate in faculty and campus committees, attend faculty assembly and school meetings, and conduct program and class assessments in accordance with standards developed by the University and outside accrediting entities. Faculty are also expected to develop educational programs to be presented to the campus at large as part of the University LEAD program and to attend such programs sponsored by other faculty in the University. We are hiring for an Assistant or Associate Professor of Communication - Rank and salary are commensurate with qualification and experience. $50,000 - $58,000 WWU provides employees and their dependents with an opportunity to enroll in undergraduate, masters or doctoral coursework for credit at the university at a free or reduced cost. Employees interested in undergraduate degrees are eligible upon completion of three months of service. Masters or doctoral (including EDS) level degrees begins upon completion of six months of service. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Teach lower and upper-division undergraduate communication courses including but not limited to: sports communication, speech, communication theory, argument and debate, and media ethics. ·       Assist students with academic advising. ·       Prepare course syllabi for assigned courses that meet the needs of students and university requirements. ·       Participate in the development of assessments and evaluation of courses and the program for continuing improvement. ·       Maintain professional development according to personal and professional need. ·       Assist in recruitment efforts for the program by participating in university recruitment events and communicating with interested students. ·       Responsible for maintaining relationships with alumni of the program. Collaborate in curriculum design and materials development for the Communication program. Other duties as assigned may include, but are not limited to: ·       Other duties assigned by the Dean of the School of Art, Design, and Media. ·       Duties are subject to change based on the applicant's skills and department needs. Position Requirements: · Degree requirements preferred Ph.D. (or Terminal Degree) or M.A. in a related field · Ability to perform teaching, administrative, and clerical duties independently to fulfill goals and objectives of the program within the overall mission of the department, the division, and the University. · Teaching experience at a higher educational institution is preferred. · Demonstrated commitment to professional development, strong work ethic, and a commitment to working well with others. · Knowledge of and demonstrated experience with integrating instructional technology into classroom experiences. Typical Physical Demands: · Ability to climb several flights of stairs several times each day. · Ability to lift, push or pull up to 20 pounds. · Ability to sit or stand for long periods. · Ability to speak and read English fluently. · Ability to hear. · Ability to travel. · Must possess a valid Missouri driver’s license and adhere to the WWU vehicle policy. Work Schedule: This is a full-time, 9-month position beginning January 2027. This position will be open until filled. Qualified applicants must submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, statement of teaching philosophy, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and contact information for three references (one being a supervisor). William Woods University promotes a student-centered learning environment valuing inclusion, creativity, and intellectual inquiry.  Focused on professions-oriented education, we prepare learners for success. William Woods University is an independent institution chartered by the State of Missouri with main campus facilities in Fulton, MO.  It has been operating continuously since 1870, taking its current form as a coeducational university with undergraduate and graduate programs in 1993.  \n\n\t\t\t\tToday, William Woods draws approximately 2,000 undergraduate and graduate students from 35 states and approximately 11 foreign countries.  William Woods has been ranked as a Top 100 Midwest University by U.S. News and World Report, and has been recognized for the quality and affordability of its online degree programs.  \n\n\t\t\t\tWith a full liberal arts curriculum, William Woods also offers a strong professional tradition, with nationally ranked programs in Equestrian Studies and American Sign Language. Its graduate education program figures strongly in the administration and leadership of Missouri's state school system.  \n\n\t\t\t\tWilliam Woods University is governed by a self-perpetuating board of trustees, and remains committed to serving the public good by helping students link intellectual development with the responsibilities of citizenship and professional life. William Woods University is an Equal Opportunity Employer Back to top William Woods University One University Ave Fulton, MO 65251 800.995.3159 flourish! Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Twitter Submit feedback or report an issue with this website. William Woods University © 1870- 2026"
    },
    "https://portals.williamwoods.edu/employment/job_details.aspx?id=247": {
      "title": "Assistant-Associate Professor Cybersecurity & CIS",
      "description": "Job Details | William Woods University Skip to content Admissions\n                    Menu Job Details Job Title: Assistant-Associate Professor Cybersecurity & CIS Department: School of Business and Technology Reports To: Executive Dean, School of Business and Technology Job Type: This is a full time, exempt position. General Description: William Woods University is accepting applications for one full-time, tenure-track faculty position to teach cybersecurity (CSS), computer information systems (CIS), and related courses at the undergraduate level. The position begins in August 2026. Teaching areas may include Enterprise Systems, Systems Analysis, hardware/software support, the impact of artificial intelligence, machine learning fundamentals, human-computer interaction, business analytics, Python, programming logic and syntax, emerging technologies, Introduction to Cybersecurity, Cybersecurity Law and Ethics, Cybersecurity and Internet Architecture, Cyber Attacks and Defenses, Encryption Techniques, Social Engineering, Critical Infrastructures, Cloud Security, Cloud Computing, Database Management Systems, Networking, Project Management, and other related courses. The contracted teaching load is 12 hours per semester, with the opportunity to teach summer and intersession courses. Full-time faculty are expected to participate in faculty and campus committees, attend faculty assemblies and school meetings, and conduct program and class assessments in accordance with standards established by the University and by external accrediting entities. Faculty are also expected to develop educational programs for presentation to the campus at large as part of the University LEAD program and to attend programs sponsored by other faculty within the University. Rank and salary are commensurate with qualifications and experience. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Teach cybersecurity and computer information systems courses in the classroom and online modalities. Assist students with academic advising. Assist in internship supervision, including identifying opportunities, mentoring, and evaluating internships. Prepare course syllabi for assigned courses that meet the needs of students and accreditation requirements. Participate in the development of assessments and evaluation of courses and the program for continuing improvement. Maintain professional development according to personal and professional needs. ? Assist in recruitment efforts for the program by participating in university recruitment events and communicating with interested students. Other duties as assigned. Position Requirements: A master's degree in cybersecurity, computer information systems, or a directly related discipline (with at least 18 graduate credit hours in cybersecurity or computer information systems) is required. Ability to perform teaching, administrative, and clerical duties independently to fulfill the program's goals and objectives within the overall mission of the department, the school, and the university. Teaching experience at a higher educational institution is preferred but not required. Work Schedule: This is a full-time, 9-month position that begins in the fall of 2026 and continues into the following academic year.  This position will be open until filled. Qualified applicants must submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, and contact information for three references. William Woods University is an independent institution chartered by the State of Missouri with main campus facilities in Fulton, MO.  It has been operating continuously since 1870, taking its current form as a coeducational university with undergraduate and graduate programs in 1993.  \n\n\t\t\t\tToday, William Woods draws approximately 2,000 undergraduate and graduate students from 35 states and approximately 11 foreign countries.  William Woods has been ranked as a Top 100 Midwest University by U.S. News and World Report, and has been recognized for the quality and affordability of its online degree programs.  \n\n\t\t\t\tWith a full liberal arts curriculum, William Woods also offers a strong professional tradition, with nationally ranked programs in Equestrian Studies and American Sign Language. Its graduate education program figures strongly in the administration and leadership of Missouri's state school system.  \n\n\t\t\t\tWilliam Woods University is governed by a self-perpetuating board of trustees, and remains committed to serving the public good by helping students link intellectual development with the responsibilities of citizenship and professional life. William Woods University is an Equal Opportunity Employer Back to top William Woods University One University Ave Fulton, MO 65251 800.995.3159 flourish! Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Twitter Submit feedback or report an issue with this website. William Woods University © 1870- 2026"
    },
    "https://portals.williamwoods.edu/employment/job_details.aspx?id=378": {
      "title": "Assistant-Associate Professor of Exercise Science",
      "description": "Job Details | William Woods University Skip to content Admissions\n                    Menu Job Details Job Title: Assistant-Associate Professor of Exercise Science Department: School of Science and Health Reports To: Dean, College of Science and Health Job Type: This is a full time, exempt position. General Description: William Woods University is accepting applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position to teach exercise science to undergraduate students. The contracted teaching load is 12 hours per semester, with the opportunity to teach additional courses as overload. Full-time faculty are expected to participate in faculty and campus committees, attend faculty assembly and school meetings, and conduct program and class assessments in accordance with standards developed by the University and outside accrediting entities. Faculty are also expected to develop educational programs to be presented to the campus at large as part of the University LEAD program and to attend such programs sponsored by other faculty in the University. Rank and salary are commensurate with qualification and experience. WWU provides employees and their dependents with an opportunity to enroll in undergraduate, masters or doctoral coursework for credit at the university at a free or reduced cost. Employees interested in undergraduate degrees are eligible upon completion of three months of service. Masters or doctoral (including EDS) level degrees begins upon completion of six months of service. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: · Teach lower and upper-division undergraduate exercise science courses. · Assist students with academic advising. · Prepare course syllabi for assigned courses that meet the needs of students and university requirements. · Participate in the development of assessments and evaluation of courses and the program for continuing improvement. · Maintain professional development according to personal and professional need. · Assist in recruitment efforts for the program by participating in university recruitment events and communicating with interested students. · Responsible for maintaining relationships with alumni of the program. Collaborate in curriculum design and materials development for the Exercise Science program. Other duties as assigned may include, but are not limited to: · Other duties assigned by the Dean of the College of Science and Health. · Duties are subject to change based on the applicant's skills and department needs. Position Requirements: A doctoral degree in exercise science is preferred, however, an experienced educator with a master’s or ABD in exercise science will also be considered. ·       Ability to perform teaching, administrative, and clerical duties independently to fulfill goals and objectives of the program within the overall mission of the department, the College of Science and Health, and the University. ·       Teaching experience at a higher educational institution is preferred. ·       Demonstrated commitment to professional development, strong work ethic, and a commitment to working well with others. Work Schedule: This is a full-time, 9-month position beginning August 2026. This position will be open until filled. Qualified applicants must submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, statement of teaching philosophy, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and contact information for three references (one being a supervisor). William Woods University promotes a student-centered learning environment valuing inclusion, creativity, and intellectual inquiry.  Focused on professions-oriented education, we prepare learners for success. William Woods University is an independent institution chartered by the State of Missouri with main campus facilities in Fulton, MO.  It has been operating continuously since 1870, taking its current form as a coeducational university with undergraduate and graduate programs in 1993.  \n\n\t\t\t\tToday, William Woods draws approximately 2,000 undergraduate and graduate students from 35 states and approximately 11 foreign countries.  William Woods has been ranked as a Top 100 Midwest University by U.S. News and World Report, and has been recognized for the quality and affordability of its online degree programs.  \n\n\t\t\t\tWith a full liberal arts curriculum, William Woods also offers a strong professional tradition, with nationally ranked programs in Equestrian Studies and American Sign Language. Its graduate education program figures strongly in the administration and leadership of Missouri's state school system.  \n\n\t\t\t\tWilliam Woods University is governed by a self-perpetuating board of trustees, and remains committed to serving the public good by helping students link intellectual development with the responsibilities of citizenship and professional life. William Woods University is an Equal Opportunity Employer Back to top William Woods University One University Ave Fulton, MO 65251 800.995.3159 flourish! Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Twitter Submit feedback or report an issue with this website. William Woods University © 1870- 2026"
